edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186345042 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0854eeb0-38e4-505f-a728-28edf544308c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345042 #edb/ref 1074 "We write down $B$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{B}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186345054 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345054 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75239" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345054 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345054 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -23 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186345054 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b3d9954a-235f-5dbc-876a-c24dd6400de2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345054 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -23 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+23{R}_{3} 